  "details": "Please add a toggle to temporarily disable the action menu via the quick menu and/or the action menu itself that reverts automatically when (re)joining an instance, to allow players to prevent accidental opening of the action menu at inopportune times.\n\nThe action menu prevents you from moving while it's open. Factors such as controller wear, how hard you grip the controller, and use of joysticks at the extremes of their movement range make it easier to accidentally open the menu. This has been a frequent source of disruption in fast-paced gaming scenarios where player movement is vital.\n\nPlayers can work around this using an alternate binding that leaves the action menu unbound, but editing bindings is a heavy-handed approach for a use case that may require frequent toggling (e.g. between rounds within a single instance).\n\nFor clarity: \n\nAction menu is the radial menu\n\nQuick menu is the first layer of menu you get when pressing the menu button",
